113.1%; position: relative;\" data-tex=\"M\"><mjx-math class=\" MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D440 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span> is the max of all of\nthem and it works.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<div class=\"enumerate\" data-options=\"label=(\\alph*)\">\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li>Name three faults of the text, each by the convention it breaks\n(this section) or the step that is not written.</li>\n<li>Rewrite the proof at level 3.</li>\n</ol>\n</div>","file":"ch08-from-derivations-to-prose/05-writing-proofs.html"}